  "archive_id": "BW2-B74-P02",
  "title": "The v-Numbers of (x2,y2,zc,xyz) and Its Integral Closure for Every c at Least 2",
  "batch_label": "74",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every field K and every integer c >= 2, in K[x,y,z] the ideal I_c=(x^2,y^2,z^c,xyz) satisfies v(I_c)=2 and v(overline(I_c))=ceil(c/2). Consequently v(overline(I_2))<v(I_2), equality holds for c=3,4, and v(I_c)<v(overline(I_c)) holds exactly for c>=5.",
